.TH NEMUE-SCAN 1 "November 2025" "Nemue 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nemue-scan \- Network port scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nemue scan
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I TARGET

.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan network targets for open ports, detect services, and fingerprint operating systems. Supports multiple scan types, timing templates, and stealth techniques.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I TARGET
Target IP address, hostname, or CIDR range (e.g., 192.168.1.1 or 192.168.1.0/24)

.SH OPTIONS
.SS Port Specification
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-ports " " \fIPORTS\fR
Ports to scan. Can be: single (80), list (80,443), range (1-1000), or preset (common, top100, top1000). Default: 1-1000
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIPORTS\fR
Exclude specific ports from scan
.TP
.BR \-F
Fast mode (scan top 100 ports only)

.SS Scan Types
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-scan-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Scan type: syn (default), connect, udp, ack, window, null, fin, xmas, maimon
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-aggressive
Aggressive scan (enables SYN scan, service detection, OS detection, top1000 ports)
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Enable true SYN stealth scanning using raw sockets (requires root)

.SS Detection
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version-detect
Detect service versions
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-os-detect
Detect operating system
.TP
.B \-\-version-intensity " " \fI0-9\fR
Set version detection intensity (0=light, 9=all probes)
.TP
.B \-\-version-light
Quick version detection (intensity 2)
.TP
.B \-\-version-all
Try all probes (intensity 9)

.SS Timing & Performance
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rate " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum packets per second (default: 1000)
.TP
.BR \-T " " \fI0-5\fR
Timing template: 0=Paranoid, 1=Sneaky, 2=Polite, 3=Normal, 4=Aggressive, 5=Insane
.TP
.B \-\-timeout " " \fIMILLIS\fR
Timeout for each port in milliseconds (default: 1000)
.TP
.B \-\-min-rate " " \fINUM\fR
Minimum packets per second
.TP
.B \-\-max-rate " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum packets per second
.TP
.B \-\-min-rtt-timeout " " \fITIME\fR
Minimum RTT timeout (e.g., 100ms, 1s)
.TP
.B \-\-max-rtt-timeout " " \fITIME\fR
Maximum RTT timeout
.TP
.B \-\-max-retries " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum probe retransmissions
.TP
.B \-\-host-timeout " " \fITIME\fR
Give up on target after this long
.TP
.B \-\-scan-delay " " \fITIME\fR
Delay between probes
.TP
.B \-\-max-parallelism " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum parallel port scan probes

.SS Host Discovery
.TP
.B \-sn
Ping scan only (no port scan)
.TP
.B \-Pn
Skip host discovery (assume all hosts up)
.TP
.B \-PS " " \fI[portlist]\fR
TCP SYN ping
.TP
.B \-PA " " \fI[portlist]\fR
TCP ACK ping
.TP
.B \-PU " " \fI[portlist]\fR
UDP ping
.TP
.B \-PE
ICMP echo request ping
.TP
.B \-sL
List scan (just list targets, no scan)

.SS Target Specification
.TP
.B \-iL " " \fIFILE\fR
Read targets from file
.TP
.B \-iR " " \fINUM\fR
Generate random targets
.TP
.B \-\-exclude " " \fIHOSTS\fR
Exclude specific hosts
.TP
.B \-\-excludefile " " \fIFILE\fR
Exclude hosts from file
.TP
.B \-\-resolve-all
Scan all resolved addresses
.TP
.B \-\-unique
Scan each IP only once

.SS DNS Resolution
.TP
.B \-n
Never do DNS resolution
.TP
.B \-R
Always resolve (even for IPs)
.TP
.B \-\-dns-servers " " \fISERVERS\fR
Custom DNS server list
.TP
.B \-\-system-dns
Use OS resolver instead of built-in

.SS Stealth & Evasion
.TP
.B \-D " " \fIDECOYS\fR
Decoy scan with specified decoy list
.TP
.B \-S " " \fIIP\fR
Spoof source IP address
.TP
.B \-g " " \fIPORT\fR
Use specific source port
.TP
.B \-e " " \fIINTERFACE\fR
Specify network interface
.TP
.B \-\-spoof-mac " " \fIMAC\fR
Spoof MAC address
.TP
.B \-f
Fragment packets (8-byte fragments)
.TP
.B \-\-mtu " " \fISIZE\fR
Custom MTU for fragmentation
.TP
.B \-\-ttl " " \fIVAL\fR
Set IP TTL field
.TP
.B \-\-badsum
Send packets with incorrect checksums
.TP
.B \-\-proxies " " \fIURLs\fR
HTTP/SOCKS proxy chain

.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Save results to file
.TP
.B \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: json, xml, csv
.TP
.B \-\-show-closed
Show closed ports in output
.TP
.B \-\-show-filtered
Show filtered ports in output
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode (no banner)
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Display port state reasons
.TP
.B \-\-stats-every " " \fITIME\fR
Periodic statistics output

.SS Scripting
.TP
.B \-\-script-args " " \fIARGS\fR
Pass arguments to scripts
.TP
.B \-\-script-args-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Load script arguments from file
.TP
.B \-\-script-trace
Debug script execution
.TP
.B \-\-script-help " " \fISCRIPT\fR
Show script documentation

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic scan:
.B nemue scan 192.168.1.1

.TP
Scan specific ports:
.B nemue scan 192.168.1.1 -p 22,80,443

.TP
Fast aggressive scan:
.B sudo nemue scan target.com -A -T4

.TP
Stealth SYN scan:
.B sudo nemue scan target.com \-\-raw -T1

.TP
Service and OS detection:
.B nemue scan target.com -p common -V -O

.TP
Scan network range:
.B nemue scan 192.168.1.0/24 -p top100

.TP
UDP scan:
.B sudo nemue scan target.com -p 53,123,161 -s udp

.TP
Scan with decoys:
.B sudo nemue scan target.com -D RND:10

.TP
Discovery only:
.B nemue scan 192.168.1.0/24 -sn

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed successfully
.TP
.B 1
Error during scan
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nemue (1),
.BR nemue\-fuzz (1),
.BR nmap (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Nemue Project
